The rule

Every new major engine should be connected through core/trading_pipeline/pipeline.py, not directly to other engines.

For example, suppose we build a new AI engine.

❌ Bad design
ProbabilityEngine
        │
        ▼
AIEngine
        │
        ▼
SignalGenerator

Now:

Probability depends on AI.
AI depends on Signal Generator.
Signal Generator may depend on Probability.

This creates tight coupling and makes the project harder to maintain.

✅ Good design
TradingPipeline
      │
      ├── ProbabilityEngine
      ├── AIEngine
      ├── DecisionEngine
      ├── SignalGenerator
      └── RiskManager

Then inside pipeline.py:

probability = self.probability_engine.process(...)

ai_result = self.ai_engine.process(
    probability=probability,
    market_structure=market_structure,
)

signal = self.signal_generator.generate_signal(
    regime=regime,
    probability=probability,
    ai_result=ai_result,
    decision=decision,
)

Notice that:

ProbabilityEngine doesn't know AIEngine exists.
AIEngine doesn't know SignalGenerator exists.
SignalGenerator doesn't know who created ProbabilityResult.

Only the TradingPipeline knows how everything fits together.

